{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcomes — specifically, the most favorable outcome that has the minimum probability in each lottery. For Lottery A, the outcomes are -4000€ (80%) and 0€ (20%). The least probable outcome is 0€ with 20% probability, which is also the most favorable (least loss). For Lottery B, the outcome is -3000€ with 100% probability; since there is only one outcome, it is both the most and least probable. The most favorable least probable outcome in B is -3000€. Comparing the two, the reason would prefer Lottery A, because 0€ (A’s least probable outcome) is more favorable than -3000€ (B’s least probable outcome). Thus, the decision reason can be applied, and it would favor Lottery A.",
